// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_scene_capacity.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: engine/level/scene_dsl.emp's ANCHORED capacity ceiling in `scene()` — the
// first of the two guards ported by name from configs.emp's `hdr()` (spec §3.1).
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: "the shadow view needs count+1 entries — 8+1"
//
// EIGHT REAL LAYERS PLUS AN ANCHOR. Eight layers alone is legal — it is exactly
// MAX_PARALLAX_BANDS — and an anchor alone is legal. The pair is not: a world-anchored
// scene SPLITS whichever layer holds the anchored line at runtime, so the shadow view
// needs count+1 entries and the ninth writes past `Parallax_Shadow_Bands`.
//
// EVERY OTHER GUARD IN scene() PASSES, deliberately, so the lane's diagnostic count means
// something:
//   - `count >= 1 && count <= 8` — 8 is the ceiling, not past it.
//   - `anchor_ch < 4` — channel 0 indexes the patch bank fine (the OTHER ported hdr()
//     guard; tripping it too would put two anchor diagnostics in one build).
//   - the pad-slot loop — `for i in 8..8` is empty, so no slot is checked and none needs
//     to be a no_layer().
//   - every `layer()` — all eight tops are inside the engine's $8000 act-axis ceiling
//     (P3 Task 7 retired the old 8-px-grid ensure and the typed 512-px span: off-grid is
//     legal now and merely FORCES per-line via scene_forces_per_line() arm 5 — a fold this
//     module never calls — while the tight span bound moved to the registry-level
//     assert_act_relative_tagged(), which this module never calls either. See
//     poison_scene_grid.emp and poison_scene_actspan.emp for those two guards' own rows.)
//
// P3 TASK 15 RE-VERIFIED THIS ROW AGAINST THE RE-GLUED TREE: Task 7 kept this guard
// byte-for-byte (capacity stays 8, the ruling in its own step list), so the P1 fixture —
// EIGHT layers PLUS an anchor, needing nine shadow entries, exactly ONE over the ceiling
// — is still the one-unit poison for "capacity under re-glue plus an anchor" and a second
// module here would be a duplicate row, not new coverage.
//   - both raw bridges default to -1 (derive) and both selectors default to 0.
// The ONLY thing wrong with this scene is that it wants nine shadow entries.
//
// THE ELABORATION HOOK. A comptime fn is only elaborated when it is CALLED and an
// unreferenced const is inert, so the guard under test runs because this module-level
// ensure reads the const and forces `scene()`'s body. The predicate is trivially true
// against what `scene()` returns ANYWAY (`ensure` is non-aborting, so the constructor
// still hands back the Scene it built); this ensure's own message is what you would see
// if the poison ever stopped reaching its target.
//
// THE GLOB IMPORTS ARE THE AUTHOR'S OWN SPELLING — see poison_scene_grid.emp's header.
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_scene_capacity

use engine.level.scene_dsl.*
use engine.level.parallax_dsl.*

const POISON_CAPACITY_SCENE: Scene = scene(
    layers: [ layer(world_y: 0,  fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2),
              layer(world_y: 8,  fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2),
              layer(world_y: 16, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2),
              layer(world_y: 24, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2),
              layer(world_y: 32, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2),
              layer(world_y: 40, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2),
              layer(world_y: 48, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2),
              layer(world_y: 56, fa: FACTOR_1, fb: FACTOR_1_2) ],
    count: 8, v_factor: 3,
    anchor: SceneAnchor.At(0, 15, 2))

ensure(POISON_CAPACITY_SCENE.sc_count == 8,
       "poison_scene_capacity: the fixture scene no longer carries eight real layers — this poison no longer reaches the guard it targets")
